1. High-level DTH architecture
Core pieces:
• DTH Orchestrator
	◦ Role: Routes tasks to the right agent, keeps minimal history, enforces “mission scope” per agent.
	◦ Inputs: Your natural language requests.
	◦ Outputs: Calls to:
		▪︎ Personal Finance Agent
		▪︎ Scout Agent
		▪︎ Machine Monitor Agent
		▪︎ Geo-Politics Agent
		▪︎ AML/BSA Agent
		▪︎ Infra/Network Agent
• Agent Contracts (per agent)
	◦ Mission: One sentence purpose.
	◦ ROE (Rules of Engagement): What it can/can’t do.
	◦ Data sources: CSVs, APIs, YouTube transcripts, .gov, ACAMS, etc.
	◦ Outputs: Clear, structured JSON (metrics, flags, recommended actions).
